<Base title="Saydraft privacy — What stays on your PC" description="How Saydraft handles local speech, model downloads, History, optional audio retention, and a website without tracking analytics.">
  <main id="main" class="document container"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy, in plain words</p><h1>A private<br /><em>train of thought.</em></h1>
    <h2>Speech and cleanup stay local</h2><p>The app runs speech recognition and optional AI cleanup on your PC. There is no cloud transcription or account. The app does not send telemetry or crash uploads. Its runtime network guard blocks external connections outside explicit model downloads; the local cleanup server uses loopback on your own machine.</p>
    <h2>Downloads are explicit</h2><p>Models and runtimes are downloaded only when you start setup. Sizes and licenses are shown before download, and pinned files are checked with SHA-256. Installed models are reused offline. Optional update checking is off by default.</p>
    <h2>Your local History</h2><p>Dictations are saved locally in History. You can review and delete them. Audio retention is off by default; keeping recordings is a separate choice. Dictionary correction learning is also optional and off by default. The app avoids password fields.</p>
    <h2>Verify offline behavior</h2><ol><li>Finish downloading your selected models.</li><li>Disconnect your network and dictate in a plain text editor.</li><li>For a closer look, use Windows Resource Monitor to inspect Saydraft’s connections while you dictate. A local cleanup server may appear as a loopback connection.</li></ol><p>Source code and the network guard are available in the <a href="https://github.com/tanzir71/saydraft/tree/main/saydraft/privacy">public repository</a>.</p>
    <h2>This website</h2><p>This site has no tracking analytics, advertising, or microphone access. Fonts and scripts are self-hosted. Examples are canned simulations. Following an external link takes you to another service. GitHub Pages hosts the site and may process request information under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
